  "questions": [
    {"id":1,"difficulty":"Easy","question":"A car travels the same fixed distance to work every day, but at a different speed each day depending on traffic. What is the changing variable across days?","options":["The distance to work","The speed of travel","The destination","The car's fuel type"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Since distance is fixed, the variable that changes day to day is the speed of travel."},
    {"id":2,"difficulty":"Easy","question":"A store sells the same product every day at a fixed price, but the number of units sold differs daily. What is the changing variable here?","options":["The price of the product","The number of units sold","The product itself","The store's location"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Since price stays fixed, the variable that changes daily is the number of units sold."},
    {"id":3,"difficulty":"Easy","question":"A student studies for a fixed number of hours every day, but covers a different number of topics each day depending on difficulty. What is the changing variable?","options":["The number of hours studied","The number of topics covered","The student's name","The subject being studied"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Since study hours are fixed, the variable that changes is the number of topics covered."},
    {"id":4,"difficulty":"Medium","question":"A factory produces the same type of toy every day using the same machine, but the number of workers present varies daily, causing daily output to differ. Which variable changes, ultimately affecting the daily toy output?","options":["The type of toy produced","The machine being used","The number of workers present","The factory's location"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Since the toy type and machine are fixed, the varying number of workers is the changing variable driving output differences."},
    {"id":5,"difficulty":"Medium","question":"A runner completes the same 5 km route every morning, but their finish time is different each day due to varying fitness and weather. If the route length is fixed, what is the primary changing variable being tracked here?","options":["The distance of the route","The runner's finish time","The runner's name","The time of day they start"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Since the route distance is constant, the variable that changes and is being tracked is the runner's finish time."},
    {"id":6,"difficulty":"Medium","question":"A company keeps the same product price throughout the year, but total monthly revenue changes each month. Given the price is fixed, what changing variable is driving revenue differences?","options":["The number of units sold each month","The price per unit","The company's name","The accounting method used"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Since price is fixed, revenue differences must come from the changing number of units sold each month."},
    {"id":7,"difficulty":"Hard","question":"A delivery company keeps the same base fee and per-kilometer rate for all deliveries, but the total bill for each delivery differs. Given both the base fee and the rate remain fixed across deliveries, what is the changing variable causing bill differences?","options":["The base fee amount","The per-kilometer rate","The distance traveled for each specific delivery","The delivery company's name"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Since the fee and rate are fixed, the distance traveled for each unique delivery is what varies and drives bill differences."},
    {"id":8,"difficulty":"Hard","question":"A bakery sells the same three baked goods (bread, cake, cookies) at fixed individual prices every day. However, daily total revenue varies. If prices for all three items never change, which combination of variables is actually changing day to day to cause revenue differences?","options":["The prices of the three items","The number of item types sold","The bakery's name","The quantity sold of each of the three items, which can vary independently day to day"],"correctIndex":3,"explanation":"Since prices are fixed, revenue differences must come from the varying quantities sold of each item, which can change independently."},
    {"id":9,"difficulty":"Hard","question":"A school's total exam pass rate changes every year, even though the passing score threshold has remained fixed for the past 5 years. Given the threshold hasn't changed, what is the changing variable responsible for the differing pass rates?","options":["The passing score threshold","The students' performance levels each year","The name of the exam","The exam's fixed format"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Since the threshold is fixed, the varying pass rates must be driven by changes in how students actually perform each year."},
    {"id":10,"difficulty":"Hard","question":"A city's total tax revenue changes every year, even though the tax rate percentage has remained exactly the same for a decade. Given the tax rate hasn't changed, what is the changing variable most directly responsible for the differing revenue?","options":["The total taxable income/economic activity in the city each year","The tax rate percentage","The city's name","The tax collection method"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Since the rate is fixed, changes in total revenue must come from changes in the underlying taxable income or economic activity each year."}
  ]
